      "transcript_text": "Okay. Now, in addition to sole proprietorship, partnership and corporation kinds of businesses, we also have some hybrid forms of business organisation. So, there are some hybrids which combine features of one form with those of them. Another form. For example, if we talk about limited liability partnership or LLP, what is an LLP? An LLP combines the features of a partnership kind of a business with that of a corporation kind of a business. You remember, in the case of a partnership kind of a business, the liability of the partners is unlimited. However, in the case of an LLP, your limited partners have limited liability. An LLP is a separate legal entity with perpetual existence and limited liability for limited partners. Let us also very briefly talk about another hybrid which is called as one person company or OPC in short. What is an OPC? An OPC is a hybrid of a sole proprietorship and a corporation. Here, in the case of an OPC, it offers limited liability to its sole member, to its sole shareholder. However, this also has disadvantages. The disadvantage is that an OPC is taxed like a corporation. is regulated under the Indian Companies Act 2013.",
