          "correct_index": 1,
          "difficulty": "Easy | Conceptual",
          "explanation": "The correct answer is B. The lecture explicitly explained that because the coupon rate and face value do not change, the coupon payments period after period remain the same for a fixed number of periods. This pattern, same payment period after period for a fixed duration, is the definition of an annuity. The lecture then stated that we know how to find the present value of an annuity. Distractor A (Perpetuity) is wrong because a perpetuity involves payments that continue forever into infinity, whereas a bond has a fixed maturity date. Distractor C (Single lump sum) is wrong because the bond makes multiple periodic payments, not just one. Distractor Growing perpetuity is wrong because the payments are not growing; they are fixed.",
