      "transcript_text": "Let us look at one example to understand stock valuation by comparables. Now let us look at this particular table. So this table shows you stock price, price to earnings ratio and price to book ratio for two different companies, and HUL as of April 20, 2026. This data was taken from money control all this day. Now you understand that, in forces is a listed firm. For a moment, let us say that we do not know the stock price of in forces and we want to find out the stock price. The question is, can we find out the stock price of in forces using valuation by comparables approach? The answer is yes. Okay. So what is the first step? As we discussed previously, the first step is to identify comparables. So we have to identify comparables of in forces. In forces as you know, it is into IT services industry. So we have to look at those companies which are in IT services industry. So those firms which are in IT services industry will essentially be the comparables for in forces. I have taken TCS, HCL Technologies and Vipro as comparables for in forces. Of course, you might argue that there are many companies which are in IT services industry. So therefore, why have I selected only three comparables of in forces? The reason is simple. I am not just looking at those firms which are in IT services industry. I am also looking at those firms which are comparable in size to in forces. So therefore, TCS, HCL Technologies and Vipro, they are comparable to in forces because all of these are big IT services firms. What was our second step? Our second step was to choose a suitable multiple for valuation. And here we are choosing price to earnings ratio as our multiple. Now let us go to our third step. So what is our third step? Our third step was to find out the mean or the median value of the chosen multiple for our comparables which means that we have to find mean price to earnings ratio for comparables of in forces. And if you find out the mean value that essentially comes out as 19.54. Now let us move on to our last step. So in the last step, we can find out the stock price of in forces assuming that in forces will have a similar P ratio as that of its comparables. So therefore, we can say that stock price of in forces is going to equal mean of price to earnings ratio for comparables of in forces which means IT services firms into earnings per share of in forces. Okay now, if you did not know about the stock price of in forces, how could you estimate it? Given that in forces earnings per share for financial year that ended on 31 March 2026 was rupees 68.97. Can you find out the stock price of in forces given this information? Yes, we can. We understand that mean price to earnings ratio for comparables of in forces is 19.54. We understand that earnings per share of in forces as given to you as 68.97 rupees. If we find out the product of the two, we get rupees 1347.67 as our estimate of stock price for in forces. Now, you know what was the actual stock price of in forces on April 20, 2026, it was rupees 1312.60. And as you can observe, our estimate which is 1347 is not very far away from 1312 rupees. So it tells you that this approach can essentially give us a good estimate of stock price of a firm which is not listed.",
