      "transcript_text": "Now let us look at yet another problem. The total market value of a firm's equity is Rs 60 million and the total value of its debt is Rs 40 million. But the beta of the firm's equity is currently 1.5 and that the expected risk premium on the market is 6%. A assume for simplicity that the company's debt is risk free, that is the beta of debt is 0 and it pays no taxes. Given this information you have to find out what is the required return on the firm's stock, what is the firm's asset cost of capital and what is the discount rate for an expansion of the firm's present business. First of all, let us jot down the information and the cash flow. information which is given to us. It is given to us that market value of equity is Rs 60 million and the value of debt is Rs 40 million. Also, beta of equity has been estimated as 1.5 and the expected risk premium on the market which is Rs Rs Rs it is given to us as 6%. The risk free rate is against 6%. So which means that our RF is also 6%. Further it is given to us that the beta of debt is 0. The debt is completely risk free. In other words, the beta of debt is 0. So given this information, first of all we have to find out what is the required return on the company's stock. What shall we do? We will simply use the capital asset pricing model. So for answering this part, using capital asset pricing model we understand that RE equals RF plus beta of equity into RM minus RF. Our RF is given to us as 6%. beta of equity we know it is 1.5 into RM minus RF which is again given to us as 6%. So this will be nothing but 6% plus 9% which will give us cost of equity RE as 15%. Now let us go to part B. It says estimate the firms asset cost of capital. Now to answer part B we understand that our asset cost of capital is weighted average of the cost of debt and the cost of equity. Now RE, we already know we have computed it in part A as 15%. But what will our RDB using capital asset pricing model? Our RDB will be RF plus beta of debt into RM minus RF. Now RF is given to us as 6% beta of debt is 0 here into RM minus RF which is again 6%. So this implies that our RDB is simply equal to 6% which is also our risk free rate. So using this RD we can compute our RE. So what is our RE going to be equal to? It will be 40 divided by 40 plus 60 into RD which is 6% plus 60 divided by 40 plus 60 into RE which is 15%. Okay, what will this be? This will simply be 0.4 into 6% plus 0.6 into 15%. Okay, what will you get here? If you solve this you will get 11.4% as your RE. So your asset cost of capital is 11.4%. Now let us go to our last part. It says what is the discount rate for an expansion of the firms present business? What is it? The discount rate for a project as you know depends on the project risk. Now the expansion of the company's present business carries the same risk as the risk of companies assets. And therefore the asset cost of capital which we have just computed as 11.4% is going to be the appropriate discount rate.",
