      "transcript_text": "The second framework is a deeper dive into the strategic drivers of a family firm's behaviour. This refers to the goals, governance and resources of a family business. It also gives us a better understanding of the strategic alignment within the family business. The goals, governance and resources of a family firm are typical to a family business and again very unique to every family firm. The goals of a family firm are broadly to. One is the financial and second is a non-economic or the social emotional goals that the family has. Second is the governance. This refers to the structures that the family has. The family firm has put in place to ensure an alignment between both the family's goals as well as the business goals. It could also include the broader entrepreneurial family galaxy in how the governance structure flows across the different vehicles of wealth for the entrepreneur family. The third is the resources which include the familyliness as a unique bundle of resources as well as the generic non-tradables that add unique value for the family business. So, to put it simply, the family firms goals, governance resources framework captures the strategic conduct and performance which are shaped by the dynamic interplay between what the family wants, which is the goals, how the decisions are made, which is the governance and what unique assets are. And what unique assets they can leverage which is the resources.",
