      "transcript_text": "The Goals of Family Business can be viewed as a two-dimensional diagram. On one side we can look at the goal as being economic and non-economic. On the other we can look at them as being family-oriented or non-family-oriented. This gives us four quadrants within the goal. The family-oriented economic goals would include maintenance and protection of the family control over the firm. And, relatedly, also to increase the family's financial wealth. The family-oriented non-economic goals would include the creation and maintenance of family harmony, ensuring the family's reputation and social status are protected and enhanced. And, maintaining a positive family's identification with the firm. The non-family-oriented economic goals would include growth of the firm and improvements in the firm's performance itself. Because, these are not directly related to the family objective and that place through the family's control and increasing of the family's wealth. The non-family-oriented, economic goals would include creation and maintenance of a positive environment and security within the firm, the nurturing of internal and external relationships with the extended broader stakeholders including the local community and the government in many instances and making a positive impact on the community. Together these four quadrants capture the economic and non-economic family oriented and non-family oriented goals of a family business.",
