      "transcript_text": "Let's delve deeper into the dynamics of a family business. Families and businesses are two very powerful systems that have driven the history of human civilization itself. And when we talk about family businesses, we are talking about bringing these two different systems together. So, we think about these family systems and business systems. These are an overlap or are they too very separate systems by themselves. So, I actually hear we are talking of two very distinct systems, but also very interconnective systems. These are not two that can separate, function separately in a family business. The boundaries in this are not as clear as you can see. a non-family business. In a non-family business, it is clear. There is nothing from the dinner that goes to the road room and vice versa. These are two separate systems. But in a family business, the lines are not so clear. There is a lot of interconnection, there is a lot of haze in between, something is moved from here to this and vice versa. What happens as a result of it is the relationship that exists between these two systems are not simple. They are quite complex and multi-dimensional. They are players, multiple players in the family who are part of the business. And therefore, the decisions taken in the business can have an impact on the family at multiple levels. So, the relationships that exist between family and business are multi-dimensional. So, then I can look at family businesses as a larger system. That is kind of an interconnected system between these two systems. very distinct systems by themselves. Correct. Two systems, family system, business system and interconnection between the two.",
