      "transcript_text": "On the other side we have the business system and the business system is focusing on the business dimension and looking at the rules, policies, procedures which are very relevant in order to run the business. The expectations and how it is structured, everything is very different in comparison to the family business. So what does a business system look for? business system looks at things that want to make the business successful profitable growing. They will usually start from customer first and understand what their customers want. What is the problem that they are solving for their customers? What means of their customers are addressing? And as the customer evolves they will try to find out how they should evolve to keep pace with what the customer needs. So that is the first and most. The customer requirements as long as they are meeting customer needs, they know the business. They know the business business will keep growing. So I think that is where it starts. The other focus is on any business they will first keep saying what can I do for increasing my shareholder value. While in this case the shareholder is also the owner here in the family. But that is a typical business would like to say that how will I optimize my growth, how can I better my business performance? Business performance can be measured by revenue and business performance. So if you buy profits, the number of places they are in can be the amount of investments they are doing, how efficiently they are doing. So all this is the way the business would measure itself. And that is what they will look. On the people side it is different. As different from the family. We spoke about how family will want the family members to get employed and there is a natural expectation for them to take on. The perspective of the competences. The business on the other side looks really for talent. Talent that will help them meet market requirements. Talent that will help them grow. They will place importance on performance management. They will place importance to merit to qualifications. You conventional education matters more than what you have learnt at the shop. Yes. So that is the way a business will look for. And the focus also is on driving the results and the outcomes at the business level. And I am looking to maximize the business value. So even the people's incentives are also structured in that direction. So business performance, people performance go hand in hand there in a business side. The family side both are not linked at all. The irrespective of how the business performs. Good or bad. All the family members performance should be equally taken up and their increase, their bonuses, everything, whatever that you are entitled to should be the same. While business it can be disproportionate depending on your performance. And there is also the general hierarchy of authority. You have the management structure. And there is a very clear demarcation of who is senior, who is junior. And the pay grades vary according to that. The bonus structures vary. And therefore these are two very contrasting systems in themselves. And the business system is more oriented towards strengthening the business and everything that is required to work in that way. So the business has its own expectation of itself as a business. But the business is also expected to meet the requirements of the family government.",
