      "transcript_text": "So, given these two very different systems that a family business is trying to manage and balance the family system and the business system, it is only natural to expect that family businesses would vary along a spectrum of which one they prioritize. Is it a family first philosophy driving the family business or a family business? Or a business first philosophy driving a family business? And therefore, we could use that distinction to understand what would characterize a family business which is driven by a family first philosophy. A family first philosophy if a family business were to follow, they will place more importance on the requirements of the family. Like we spoke, that will mean they will require their stability, they will require their life's style support. So, what is the impact? Let us take lifestyle support, which means they will say that their income that they will keep getting should be sacrosanct. Now, the business should not touch that. So, I should get my monthly income, I should get my dividends and predictably I should get so much. Therefore, their lifestyle is not hindered in any way, that is what they will look at. Relationships are important, hierarchy is important and nothing that on these matters, they are not important. They should be interfered with by the business side of things. And also there would be an expectation that all the family members are employed and performance appraisal also would be pretty much meaningless in these contexts. As long as the business is able to sustain and support the family, performance appraisal per se would be of less importance than what we would see in a traditional business system per se. Also, what will happen is that the growth of a family, family members in the business is linked more to age and hierarchy, not to talent and skill. So, you will find that cousins who have joined together of the same age all get promoted in one year, they cannot happen across different tiers, all of them will get a different, same pay, that is how it is and how long they have been in the business that matters a lot more. Also, distinction between what happens is a non-family employee is also expected to show loyalty, But he will do work which goes beyond what his corporate job description will say. He is an employee not just of the family business but also of the family. Exactly. That is what will happen. So you will find the security guard in the factory also doubles up as the person who goes and gets the kids from the school and drives the vehicle and does the pickup job or even buys vegetables if required. So there is no one size which can say that you have to follow the JD. Yes. That is what happens in a family first kind of situation. And the discretion of the patriarch in decision making or the family member who is currently running the family business. Their discretion and their wishes of the family per se. They become very of paramount importance rather than what the business requires at that point also those the decisions taken by the patriarch are never questioned. It is almost a cycle age to say that you know I am questioning what the patriarch has decided they will not do that. Loyalty to whatever I decide is important because you are protecting the family first. So that is a system that you want to protect at all costs as long as the business is in order to run. And what about family businesses which prioritize business first kind of an approach? That is a very different system because the business will priority performance. Business gives importance to talent, to skills, to the business requirements which are customer requirements, profitability, revenue, growth. These are important metrics for the business. So only that those kind of people those kind of decisions will be taken by the business which prioritizes these. And they can have a different kind of an impact on the family. Which also could lead to family conflicts. If a prioritized business needs above family requirements and it take decisions in order to strengthen the business rather than with the objective to preserve family harmony. It could lead to family conflicts. So for example the business decision could be saying that this is a bad year. Let me not you know give you the same amount of salaries that you got last year or not give you anyone in the family a high-cres here. And reinvest whatever profits or little profits we have back into the business. It has an impact on the family lifestyle support that we talked about that may go down lower this year which means people can't take their holidays or they can't spend the way we want. So there will be a situation where some people still might spend from saving but it will not be seen that way. It is seen as they have got something more from the family from the business than we have not got is there some favoritism being happening somewhere down the line. These are questions that prop up in the family and that lead to again disharmony that we talk about. But in general the business first kind of family businesses their policies procedures rules norms. This would typically reflect a non-family own business more reflective of the industry standards rather than the unique familyliness of that particular family. True so they will they will place importance like I said merit to performance and to results rather than more input metrics. And in reality to effectively strengthen the family business you kind of need an optimum balance between these two philosophies right. Having a family first philosophy can sometimes become detrimental for the business and having a business first philosophy seems to lead to potential conflicts within the family. But these are two very important systems that the family business needs to balance. Yes sorry that is the balance is important finding that balance is not easy it is like easier said than done. Families understand this business the family business as a whole understands this usually. they know that if both are not given importance and one of them can cause problems for others like you said they are very very interconnected. So they take time to find the balance at the same time there are some strict they will go by what is a no go first. What should be avoided is clear more clear usually than what can be done. So for example they will never create disharmony in the family that will fundamentally take away the result of succession in the family and longevity of the family business. So some no go are very very clear usually and they will avoid that the rest of it they will find balance as to what works between them. And over a period of time a strong family business needs to find that balance right you need to continue to strengthen the business system while at the same time maintaining a harmony. So systems and practices evolve over a period of time and people adjust. One thing is something that family business understand like an even incorporate they say top line solves many problems. So as long as the business grows the family issues can be somehow resolved like I said there is money on the table there is money something that can be taken back home. The basic needs social security needs are all met then you are only talking of higher order needs that are required they can be managed somehow. But as long as there is growth so that is one thing that family is understand very well.",
