      "transcript_text": "So, we have discussed three kinds of family philosophies, family first, business first and a balanced view. Let us look at what is the impact of this philosophy of each philosophy on the business decisions. Let us look at entry rules as in who can enter the business, and who can join the business. In a business first kind of a scenario, only those people can join the business if they have adequate skills for the specific role that they are applying for, qualification matters. In a family first, you just need to be relative. As long as you are relative, you can join the business. Close other relative, easier to join the business and that is the rule that works. In a family enterprise spirit, what we can otherwise call as a balanced view, opportunities will be given for all individuals within the family based on the needs of the business. And to some extent, whether you have the skills for the job and that is how a balanced view will look at it. Let us take compensation. In a business first kind of a philosophy, it will be based on your JD and the market conditions. Also depends on the kind of demand and supply that exists in the market. The pay will vary in the market and that will also reflect in the business. But in a family first kind of a scenario, the pay has to be equal for somebody in the same generation. So, it will vary by generation, it will vary by age. Possibly the elder brother can get a little more than a younger brother. But if you are all cousins, you better get the same pay. Somebody in the next generation will automatically get a lower pay than the earlier generation. It is dependent on hierarchy, it is dependent on age. In a family enterprise, this is something where the family agrees as to what is an acceptable standard for everyone and sets some rules into what can be offered as pay at what levels and skills also are taken into consideration there. Let us take stock ownership. In a business first kind of a thing, stock is shared basis, the contribution to the company and how good your performance is sometimes. And stock is also shared among even non family members in a business first kind of a scenario can be shared. But in a family first, the stock is always equal by branch of the family. In a generation, if there are multiple branches, each branch will get the same level of stock holding. Performance skills do not matter here. However, in a family enterprise spirit, equal values for all are shared. Some in form of stock, some in the form of other opportunities or investments. These are what are the vehicles that are used in a balanced view in a family business form. Titles and responsibility authority. In a business, they are completely based on merit. They are completely based on who can contribute what to the business and there is only one boss in the business. There is a hierarchy is pretty clear. However, in a family business, in a family first kind of a philosophy, the titles are all the same for everyone in the same generation. And decision making is not so unitary in nature that everyone has one boss. In the end, while you may have two one generation above you, the patriarch of the business will have the final say. Indirectly, everyone in the business reports that one patriarch. That is the kind of a hierarchy that runs in a family first kind of a system. You know, balanced view, everyone with a certain set of competence will have a certain role, will have a certain hierarchy. And these things are considered, which balance both the family and the business. In a governance situation, the business first will have a board of directors, will have a chairman of the board. There will be some independent directors on the board. So, there is a balanced view inside the board itself. The board will take actions as to what the business needs and their advice will be based on that. However, in a family first kind of thing, it does not work on decisions taken by a large amount of people. Largely taken by the patriarch and that is what whatever the patriarch one gets done. At best, it is some kind of a broad consensus that they will agree on within the family. Within that also, specific decisions will be devolved to the patriarch. Consensus is probably the best that you can expect in a family first kind of a philosophy. You know, in a balanced view, there exists more than one forum. While the decision can still be taken by the patriarch finally, there will still be something called a family council. They will be guided by all the owners in the business will have a family council will discuss it before arriving at a final decision. As far as the community role is concerned, the business first will look at the leadership role in the community. While for the family first, it is entirely a voluntary kind of a participation in the community. Balanced view will take its thing that we should be active in some areas and where there are alignment of the family, the community and the individual patriarch meets is where these things will happen. So, these are what you can see of the family philosophy, whether you look at business first, family first of balanced. How they have an impact on the overall business decisions?",
