      "transcript_text": "And, destruction is only one power, right? The other one that you mentioned, the power to create and the power to create need not come only with the founding generation. Even the subsequent generations, once the inherit, they can create new value, they can behave like an entrepreneur rather than only as a custodian. So, the power to create is again a very important. One that we need to look at. Yes, so, owners create in every generation side. The founder also creates something, he sees a vision, he understands the customer problem that he thinks he can solve and that is why he starts doing a certain goods or service and therefore, solve the certain customer problem and therefore, ribs are reward for it. Yes. But, it is still a struggle phase, correct? The second generation we talked about just now that how stability there is something already that is there, built in. There is some stability they see when they come into the business. Yes. For them, for many of them, it is also how can I leave a legacy behind? What has happened till now is my dad's legacy, right? Correct. So, it will always be known like what my dad created. Yes. I do not know if you are aware what Rishap, Meriwala said recently. How Mariko was built by my dad and at some point I realized that I have to leave behind my own legacy and I forward into something consumer business a little. It did not work. I came back. I tried something else, did not work. I was settled on investment, finally venture capital, Spark investment or something. Sharp, Sharp investment is the company name which he started and is doing that. So, they one they realize that they have to have a legacy. From there starts this idea of I have to create something also. They have the power to create. Today they have the stability to create. Yes. The wealth to create. Yes. So, Vayilun, you have saying something very interesting. He is old Tyrokar, you know. Yes. Sir, a cart of army is he and have significantly very good valuation. So, he was asked just to what is going to do about it next. What is his next step? He says he is planning something around the diagnostics area but his tight lip didn't want to reveal too much. I do not know what. He is facing right now. At one point came across he said if you have the wealth, if you have the capability and you sit and do nothing about it and try and just enjoy with what you have. It is actually a crime is what he said. It is something short of a crime. So, when Uday Kautak talks about people who have inherited a lot of wealth and sit in family offices and invest in mutual funds and they think the life of the Kautak was lamenting things. Yes. The next gen is actually busy doing mutual funds in the investors. The professional investors and head of family offices and he says that is equivalent of what the Illuminati would call a crime. So, these people have the create something. Have the power to the next generation can create. And they can change the strategic direction. Look at the reliance. It is an oil and petrochemical giant. But if you look at its current strategic direction because of the vision of the owner, it is becoming a consumer tech and retail tech giant. The entire digital investment that they have made is a completely different direction. And at one point of time if we maybe look at reliance 10 or 15 years older, we would not have imagined an oil or a petrochemical giant to be doing all of what reliance today is doing. Although there is a famous metaphor of data being the new oil. Which in reliance cases really the strategic direction, data has become their new oil. So, the owners can significantly change the direction. Often said that the word geo is actually the mirror image of the word oil. Yes. So, that is how apparently the name geo came up. It is supposed to be a story. We do not know how accurate this can be. But the fact is it is a mirror image. Similarly, we can look at the other nay group. They are entire foray into infrastructure. But if you look at the roots of the other nay family, they are from a trading background. In the infrastructure giant that we know them to be today. It is the power of the owner to create or the bajajas. You know, ditching the shithak and moving away from the shithak to building their dominance in the executive segment and the subsequent success in the two-wheeler market as we know them today. This is an entrepreneurial side of the owner and the power to create. So, for all of this, there can be other examples to how creation may not help. How will it go? For example, let us take the example of Ola. Yes. Bhavishagaraval. What started as Ola and was reasonably successful? Then he went into East Kutas. Yes. Which we do not know where that is today. How good it is doing. Then he foreade into AI and said I will build some kuthrim or something. I have to forget him. Kutrim, he built something. So, it is the power he wanted to create something. He had the power to create. He had the wealth to create after the money raised from Ola and for the East Kutram also. But yes, it is still the, can I say, judgment is not to be made so early. There is still a jury still out there. But yes, that is the power to create. He is exercising it is the point here. Will some succeed? Will all succeed? Not sure. Correct. But he has the power to create. Yes.",
