      "transcript_text": "The last stage is what is called as the Family Federation Stage. The Family Federation Stage is actually an extension of the cousin consortium stage. Where if we go into the next stage after cousins, next generation after cousins, it is still cousins, but slightly more distant and it is a very small stage. very large number. All of their individual shareholding becomes very small, very negligible. With that kind of shareholding, they can't influence anything at all. But if it is the same company that they are responsible for, then how does decisions get taken? By this stage, if a family has reached the fourth generation, what usually happens is, and if it is a large enough business that they are handling and that is how they are able to grow and continue in the future. The same business, what usually happens is the business has been hyped off into either multiple companies or they are into multiple areas. Let's say TV is group. It is a good example of a family federation. Now, there are huge number of branches that exist in a TV is group today. Each of them handles a different business. Each branch handles a different business. There is somebody handling tires, so family can TV is motors, somebody handling, syndrome fasteners, somebody handling insurance. So, TV is maybe 10 areas. So, all of them are handled by one member of the family. They have a unique, very structured where they have crossholding with the main TV as motors company also, as well as each of them have a significant share in their own company that they are handling. So, decisions are taken at this stage when it reaches, you need governance mechanism of a very high order. And that is what at this stage family is built. They don't rely on an informal just a board mechanism where they are still conflict and which can't be resolved so easily. There is a lot more, they have forum, they have family forum, they actually write down at this stage a family constitution as to what can be done, who can come into the business, who cannot, what skills are required, all detailed for a family constitution. But there are governance mechanism, there is board, there is just one governance mechanism, there is a family council that decides a lot more. So, these are mechanisms put in place for the, when the business reaches the family federation stage.",
