          "front": "Why does relationship conflict reduce satisfaction and performance regardless of the task?",
          "back": "Relationship conflict focuses on the person, not the issue. Once it enters the system, disputes persist about how someone was treated rather than what was done, creating persistent tension that distracts from all tasks."
