      "transcript_text": "Let's assume that a family business has decided to professionalize, okay. Once it decides to professionalize, what is the path it takes? So, there are 3 paths, but the solution is the same. We have to reach  a stage where a family business runs like a professional company. Let's take path 1, where family members  are are focused on. Now, this is a family which is already in the business, understands the business. When is this option best? This option is best when when the generation that is in charge of the business is very capable, or the next generation is actually a very capable generation which can take over the reins  of the company. Now, here we have touched the ability part of it. What they should also be is they should be willing to take on this role. So, this willingness-ability matrix that we spoke about earlier is very important, too. So, that's the path 1. What's path 2? Are there non-family insiders? Now, who are these non-family insiders? People who have already been in the company for a long time, confidants of the family who have earned the trust of the family members by virtue of their long service in the company. When is this suited? This suited when this kind of people who are there are also talented. There is enough talent in them, but they have always lacked the authority or exposure. For everything they have been used to going to the patriarch or the family bosses to get the approval. While they are equally good enough to take those approvals, they have never been trusted with those authorities. So, if such people exist, path 2 is an option. The last path is can we can do external hires to take the company professional. But these are professional managers from outside the company who are going to join almost new. This works best when the family needs some expertise which is lacking in the company. It is lacking both in the family members, it is lacking also in the long time, long insiders, maybe call it the long-term people who have been there in the company. Let's say it's a new technology or a new kind of science or a new market, and they really don't have the expertise or the experience to take on something like that, then we need exide then we need people from outsider from outside. So, these are not mutually exclusive. So, there can be one part of the company which, which can still be run by the family members. There's another part of the company for which we can have external hires. So,  this is not one size fit all for the entire company. This can be taken for different departments in a different way. Let's take each path in a little bit of depth. When you had take path one, where family members who are already there in the business are used to take the firm to a  professional kind of a setting. These guys have lot of years of exposure in the particular business. So, what they understand is what are the risks that are possible in this. They can understand what kind of mistakes have been done in the past and what needs to be avoided. The family, if they have demonstrated accomplishment, it is great. Otherwise what can be a risk in this kind of a situation is because they are family, there can be leniency in evaluation. We spoke about it earlier. The type 2 agency, where because they are family, they can't be promoted, they can't a-be asked to report to somebody else, and they can't be evaluated in the same way a non-family member can be evaluated. What can be a safeguard, however, is we have to demand accountability against the same criteria that would be used in case there is a professional. An example in this case is how Nisaba Godrej actually succeeded the non-family CEO Vivek Gambhir but only after building her own track record. Where a family succession that followed a professional development path first, and then the family moved in. So, it's like 2 steps. First professionalized, then the family person who by the time has picked up the skills has moved into that role. Let's take path 2, where you can professionalize using long-tenured non-family, what I call insiders. So, what these people have is very, very firm-specific knowledge because they've been for a long time inside the company. They have been part of the growth of the company and therefore understand the business very well. So, these are genuine people. These are not a risk at all. Objectivity towards the family. The non-family insider has to earn it  by the title and the mandate that that is being offered to that. External benchmarking we still need. Even for a long-tenured insider, we need to understand what should those person be evaluated on. There is trust that exists, but this is easy to skip therefore. But we should not skip it. They should be evaluated just because they are an insider they should they should be subjected to the same kind of an examination we would have dealt with in a non-family person. Example here is TK Kurien of Wipro became CEO even though Premji's family retained board control. He's a long-term insider who was promoted to the role of the CEO after having spent a long time in Wipro. The board evaluated him in the same way they would had they hired somebody else from outside for the CEO. Next string part 3, which is hiring external professional managers. These guys bring a lot of expertise. These guys have worked independently at this level outside the family. They are independently. They are they have a track record. They're well-proven. So that's what you get them for. What they don't have is a specific knowledge of our firm from day one, and  they will have to earn their trust, that takes time. They know the industry very well perhaps, but specifically how this firm works is something they'll pick up. But usually such people with a lot of skills can pick it up in a much shorter time than we expect. Where this will fit is when we have a capability gap, where we need some kind of a change to be done, we need some expertise, or we are facing some headwinds and we need a turnaround, we need some kind of a change management to be done. This is the kind of area where an expert from outside can really come and fit in.",
