          "difficulty": "Moderate | Tricky",
          "explanation": "The correct answer is B. The central thesis of the Uppsala model is that internationalisation risk is reduced through learning over time. As the firm gains knowledge about the foreign market, it can move from low-commitment modes (sporadic export, independent agent) to higher-commitment modes (sales subsidiary, FDI). The other options are incorrect because the model does not focus on government subsidies, competitor imitation, or opportunity cost as the primary driver of commitment progression.",
          "key_concept": "Uppsala Model Risk Reduction through Learning"
