          "explanation": "The transcript explains upper echelons theory: 'the younger generation, the kid has gone abroad, done his studies over there, built a professional network over there and come back. Or there are other families running their own family businesses who have internationalized in your social circle. And you're looking to them as a peer effect that you're following.'\n\n**Why correct:** This option directly quotes the mechanism described: foreign-educated younger generation and peer effects from other internationalized families.\n\n**Why distractors are wrong:** Option A (firm age) is not the focus. Option C (total assets) is not discussed as a trigger. Option D (dividend policy) is unrelated to the upper echelons trigger mechanism described.\n\n**Key Concept:** Upper Echelons Theory & Peer Effects",
