      "transcript_text": "Let's understand the process of building a family constitution Like we said, this is a very deliberative, iterative process. Coming out with a very first draft is pretty easy. Because we understand the various points that are to be there in a family constitution, right. So we can make a first draft, and that's pretty much easy. But then when we just bring this family constitution first draft to the family forum is when the discussion starts. So just like an Indian country's constitution has amendments at various points of time over its own journey, the family constitution will also need some kind of amendments with time. So let's understand each one, one by one. The starting point of a constitution can always be something as to what we are currently doing, what are we satisfied with what we are doing currently and what we are not. And as long as that can be defined to some extent, it's a good starting point to create a, a family constitution. What the writing a charter the family can agree to, some of the points that are easy and we can start this as a first step is to first create understand on what the mandate is for this constitution. What the body is or rule is actually for. What kind of members can be as part of those who are drafting the constitution? What should be the size of this group which creates this constitution? What should be their qualifications? How many members can be chosen to be part of this team which drafts the constitution for the company and the family? And you can understand as to this will take an iterative process. So what is the term limit given for the members out here who manage this constitution? What are the length of their terms, and how often do they meet? What can it decide, recommend, or what it must escalate? And how is it funded? And whether the members who are part of this drafting team get paid, not. All that can be decided initially. The next, once it is created, is the ratification step, which is basically presenting this to those with authority and getting their agreement. A well-drafted document, with the people with whom the real authority lies, they were, they are never brought into this at any point of the drafting and, and implementing of this constitution, something that will often lead to failure. Because there is no involvement, there is no deliberation with the people who genuinely wield power, and therefore, they have seen this as something that has been hoisted on them, foisted on them without their involvement, without their consent, and therefore, this is bound for failure. What the, the, the constitution drafting team should do is treat this approval from current authority holders at a very, very important and necessary step, and not see it as an afterthought, not present it when all is done, at least from their end when they think that all is done. They must be involved at every stage so that the, the final constitution draft does not face any hurdles from those who can really take decisions on whether it is to be implemented or not. Sometimes even if the forum agrees, if the owners put their foot down then the constitution is not getting anywhere. So the decision-makers must be involved at every stage. And lastly, like we spoke about how the constitution needs to be reviewed and revised. GMR is a very good example how they have set a, a, a review cycle itself. And when the constitution will be examined again by the same deliberative process that was used to build it as to how the forum which deliberated on the, on the constitution when they were first building it, led to a very iterative process. Everyone spoke about their thoughts, their requirements, and then the constitution got built, is the same way in which they have actually documented will be rewritten by a different generation or a different set of owners or whoever is in charge again at that stage. We said the persons with, with authority are important, right. So as time goes, the people holding the authority change. So the constitution will also be revised. When it is revised, has to fulfil the requirements, the requirements of those owners. So this is something that is already codified into the GMR document, and that is how a constitution will stand the test of time. And that's a very important requirement for any constitution, for any family business.",
