      "transcript_text": "There are 3 more specialized vehicles that sit between the family and the ownership's governance. Each of them exists to solve a very distinct practical problem that is that the family business faces. These are the family bank, the investment committee and the strategic planning committee. We shall look at each one of them one by one. The family bank is an internal capital allocation mechanism. And what does the investment committee do similarly, and what does the strategic planning committee do? Family itself will have multiple requirements of capital. Each family member necessarily may not be part of the business, may want to start something on their own. May want to step outside and do something else. Or maybe while still working in the company, try to do something else which is slightly adjacent or something different and start off something else. What the family bank will do is actually will encourage next generation entrepreneurship What the family bank will also do ensure that each new family member understands the financials very well, is literate on the company's financials, understands P&L, and also keeps the family capital rotating within the family system itself and ensures that even since even system goes outside, it's still the family capital that is deployed there and the returns come back into the family bank itself. That's the The primary role will still be encouraging next-generation entrepreneurship. So, what does it take to run a family bank well? What are the various elements that go into a family bank and what it has to protect itself against? It is important that the family bank has clear written eligibility criteria and clear policy that goes behind it, and the decisions that are taken of the use of   the money in the family bank is not arbitrary. It's not something based on relationship because I like somebody or dislike somebody, money can be given or not be given. There should be a formal underwriting process. What it means is if some business needs money, some venture  or a new incubated entrepreneurship venture needs money or not, money given to it should be not based on something because he's family, because, okay they need it, please let's give it to them. Should be a formal process, should be the same way market would judge on whether the money is to be given or not, basically based on merit and not because as a favor to a fellow family member. And even if a loan is given, how is the interest rate going to be calculated? It's best if it's be  calculated on market rates on something that is prevailing, that is in the market and not being given as a gift. If a loan is being classified as a gift, then well, within family members gift don't attract tax or the gift tax is at best which is which is attracted. But it means that the loan will never be repaid. The bank will never get back the money. Lastly, the key design element  in a family bank be run, it should have an independent oversight. It ensures that there is no favoritism that runs between family members in ensuring the use of funds in the family bank. And in the sense what it leads to is a loss of family trust in the process if you don't have an independent oversight. The family investment committee, what it does is, It takes away the evolution of this from whoever runs the business today to a broader branch representation, professionalized execution, and real transparency in the investment decisions of the family and the business. Today, decisions are made on the  on the investments of the family by somebody who is in charge of the business. He or she is assumed to know enough on where the family also should invest by virtue of being running the business. So from there, from one person usually who's running the business, at least in the early stages, this leads to a broader representation. The strategic planning committee is is where the parallel planning actually happens. In terms of there is a business strategic plan that is already in place, right. The business strategic plan should also take into account the family values and goals and the constraints that the family has, and therefore how the constraints will transfer into the strategic business strategic plan also. So, this is a parallel planning process in terms of the business plan and the family plan, and they  both must be in sync.",
