          "suggested_time_minutes": 15,
          "model_answer": "The three circles are the Family Circle, the Business Circle, and the Management Circle.\n\n* **Family Circle:** Governed by vehicles like the family forum, family council, and family constitution. The focus is on managing family relationships, values, and succession. \n* **Business Circle:** Governed primarily by the Board of Directors. The focus is on strategic purpose, monitoring performance, and committee composition.\n* **Management Circle:** Focuses on the day-to-day operational running of the business.\n\nIt is important to document these mechanisms and revisit them frequently because informality works only to a certain extent. As generations pass and market conditions change, the requirements of each circle evolve. Written documentation with built-in modification mechanisms ensures that the governance structures remain aligned with the family's fundamental objective of ensuring the longevity and succession of the firm.",
