          "id": 1,
          "question": "Explain why 'data never speaks for itself' is a foundational principle of critical thinking. Use the Target pregnancy prediction case study and the business analyst dashboard example to support your answer. (10 marks)",
          "marks": 10,
          "suggested_time_minutes": 15,
          "model_answer": "Data never speaks for itself because people interpret data, ask questions, and make assumptions; therefore, errors in reasoning are inevitable when people are involved. In the Target case study, statistician Andrew Pole's model was technically correct and the predictions were accurate, but the critical thinking failure was neglecting the human question of 'Should we?' and the second-order effects on trust. The model predicted pregnancy based on purchasing behavior shifts, but Target had to insert irrelevant ads (beer, lawnmowers) to hide the intrusiveness of the targeting, demonstrating that precision does not guarantee acceptability. Similarly, the business analyst dashboard example shows that a 30% increase in website traffic is real data, but the conclusion that the marketing campaign was successful may be entirely wrong if the cause was bots, technical errors, or curiosity-driven viral posts. In both cases, the numbers are real, but the interpretations depend on the critical thinking surrounding the data, not the data itself.",
