          "explanation": "The correct option is B because the lecture explains: \"The American tourist saw a friendly old man gesturing and smiling next to the thing that he wanted to buy and he believed that this is an agreement. Because agreement is what he'd come looking for.\" The American's implicit position is that Muni, being next to the clay horse, owns it and is therefore selling it. This is not based on any statement from Muni, but on the assumption that proximity equals ownership.\n\nWhy distractors are wrong:\n- A) The American believes Muni is a goatherd, not a government official. Muni, not the American, fears the official.\n- C) The American starts by bargaining for the statue; he does not assume a specific price initially. The 100 rupee note comes later.\n- D) The American is the one wanting to buy, not Muni. Muni is selling (or thinking he is selling) the goats.\n\n**Key Concept**: Implicit Position / Proximity = Ownership Assumption",
