          "explanation": "The correct option B is right because the lecture explicitly noted: \"That famous story we tell today that Netflix saw the future only emerged after the decision succeeded. The argument came first, the story came later.\" Option A is a distractor because the lecture discussed AI tools generating text, not requiring stories for data processing. Option C is a distractor because the lecture argued the opposite: stories are constructed accounts guiding perception, not necessarily more factual. Option D is a distractor as the lecture focused on the functional difference between stories and arguments, not board member preference.",
