          "explanation": "The correct option C is right because the lecture emphasized that technology has changed the speed of production, but \"what has not changed is how they should be judged.\" The standards require examining the argument underneath the polish. Option A is a distractor because polished writing can mask weak arguments; grammatical correctness does not equal logical validity. Option B is a distractor as formatting is a surface feature. Option D is a distractor as speed is irrelevant to argument quality.",
