          "explanation": "The correct answer directly quotes the professor's key takeaway: \"Good evidence isn't always enough. We have to ask whether the evidence actually supports the claim that we are making.\" Distractor A is the exact error the lecture warns against. Distractor B is the opposite of the lecture's message. Distractor D incorrectly limits the relevance of warrants.",
