          "explanation": "The correct answer is B because the lecture emphasizes that the danger of frameworks is when the user forgets they are simplified versions of reality. The examiner tests the student's understanding of the boundary condition: frameworks are tools for organization, not reflections of absolute truth. Forcing a compressed structure to act as the full truth is the exact pitfall the lecture warns against.",
          "key_concept": "Framework Utility vs. Factual Truth"
