          "explanation": "The correct option is B because the professor explicitly stated that an appeal to authority is reasonable when the authority is genuinely an expert, impartial, and relevant. It becomes a problem when invoked to shut down inquiry, when invoked in completely unrelated terms, or when used to conceal the fact that no evidence exists. Option A is a trap because title alone does not guarantee epistemic privilege. Option C is a trap because the lecture acknowledged that authority based on expertise is valid. Option D is a trap because reasonableness is not determined by majority agreement.",
