          "explanation": "Correct answer is C) The Asset Cost of Capital (RA). The lecture explicitly states: 'the expansion of the company's present business carries the same risk as the risk of company's assets, and therefore the asset cost of capital... is going to be the appropriate discount rate.' Option A is a common trap (Trap 1 in the radar), where students confuse the required return on equity with the firm-wide discount rate.",
          "key_concept": "Project Discount Rate Determination"
