          "difficulty": "Easy | Conceptual",
          "explanation": "Correct answer is B) The cost of debt (RD) equals the risk-free rate only if the beta of debt is zero. The lecture states: 'Using capital asset pricing model, our RD will be Rf plus beta of debt into Rm minus Rf. Now, RF is given to us as 6%. Beta of debt is 0 here into Rm minus Rf, which is again 6%. So, this implies that our RD is simply equal to 6%, which is also our risk-free rate.' Option A is incorrect because the lecture assumes risk-free debt. Option C misstates the CAPM application. Option D is incorrect as RD is a necessary input for RA.",
