      "transcript_text": "Now, let us talk about information content of share repurchases. Essentially, do share repurchases have any information for investors? Now, let us talk about what we see in practice. In practice, we observe that managers are much less committed to share repurchases than they are to dividend payments. Announcement of a share repurchase, therefore, is not a commitment to continue repurchases in later years. Another important observation is that unlike dividends, managers do not smooth repurchases from one year to another year. Also, managers use repurchases to often signal that the shares are undervalued. When companies offer to repurchase their shares at a premium, usually senior managers and directors commit to hold on their shares. Announcement of share repurchases at a premium to the current market price therefore leads to a positive stock price reaction.",
