          "difficulty": "Moderate | Sensitivity Analysis",
          "explanation": "The correct answer is 200 million rupees. In Scenario 3, promoters contributed 1,400 million rupees (20 million shares x Rs 70) but their market value of equity increased to 7,600 million rupees (80 million shares x Rs 95). The gain is 7,600 - (60 million shares original value + 1,400 contributed) = 200 million rupees more than their contribution. This 200 million rupees is the wealth transferred from non-participating other shareholders. Option A (128.6 million rupees) is the wealth transferred in Scenario 2, a distractor for students who do not distinguish between the two scenarios. Option C and D represent the total cash raised, not the net transfer.",
