      "transcript_text": "Now, let us move on to our last kind of seasoned equity offering, which is private placements of equity. In a private placement of equity, shares are typically issued to a small group of investors. These investors could be promoters of the firm or they could be outside investors such as private equity players, banks, financial institutions, et cetera. Now, when a firm announces a private placement of equity, the market generally reacts positively to such announcements. Here, the market means stock market. Why do you think the stock market reacts positively to announcements of private placements of equity? You understand that in a private placement of equity, large number of shares will be issued to a small number of investors. And therefore, this is going to lead to creation of what we call as block holders who will be having chunks of stake in the firm. And because they have these chunks of stake in the firm, they have incentives to monitor the managers of the firm, and also they can certify the valuation of assets of the firm. So, because of this monitoring and certification benefit, what typically happens is that when a firm announces a private placement of equity, the stock market reacts positively to these announcements. Now, what are the advantages of private placements of equity? Whenever a company makes a public offer, for example, an FPO, it is obligated to register the issue with the securities market regulator. So therefore, a company could avoid this costly process by selling the securities privately in the private placement of equity. It costs less to arrange a private placement than to make a public issue. This is a particular advantage for companies making smaller issues. However, there is one disadvantage to private placements of equity, and that disadvantage is that investors to whom the equity is placed privately, they cannot easily resell their shares. There is usually some lock-in period for such investors, and therefore these investors have to wait should they decide to sell their shares.",
