      "transcript_text": "So in Graham, Paul Graham's essay, a founder in a founder mode asks questions and pushes back hard but the target is the decision, not the person defending it. People leave those conversation having heard something even when they lost the argument. The failure mode critics point out to that the founder who asked as many hard questions but the target quietly becomes the person and not the decision. So therefore, what happens is the room and everybody in that room learns to stop bringing bad news to founders rather than argue better. So What happens is that this gets into a slightly different spin. So if you, case in point in India is Ola. Here is somebody who's in a total founder mode, and very much so. So Bhavish Aggarwal is personally involved in decision-making at multiple levels of the company. And the reports say that there is a huge senior executive turnover at roughly 13 departures over 5 years and sometimes 45% in one year. And the CEO who was hired went off in 4 months' time. If you look at Airbnb and Ola, Airbnb said when he saw the company drifting away, he started to take ownership of many decisions, and he turned around the company. On the other side, you have Ola. Because of the founder mode, the company started to have kind of a revolving door. People are coming in, staying for some time, and going out. So what it tells you is whether disagreement survives contact with the founders. In a functioning founder mode company, somebody can tell the founder they're wrong and still have a job the next morning. In a dysfunctional founder mode company, you may not be welcome or you may not get the same kind of response from the chair, from the founder. So the attrition goes up. And that is something that you can look for, right. That's the real diagnostic question. What happened when last time somebody told this founder they were making a mistake? So what happened? So you could even actually ask that question in your interview to the founder saying that, \"Do you allow people questioning you?\" And you can then look at the answers. The founder who answers with a specific story, including a time when they were wrong and changed the course, is telling you something different from a founder who answers with general philosophy about how open the door is, how open he is to criticism, how he's welcome. He is not giving you any specifics. Which means that there may actually not be specifics that have survived the confrontation they had with the founder, right. So this vague, undocumented claim is how power gets used day to day.",
