      "transcript_text": "Going back, it's not as if Saying that Bhavish Aggarwal is a bad founder Because Ola has built a very large business and they have done well. They're doing well. Current little hiccups, but they are doing well. But it tells you what kind of company you are getting into. So maybe at a level where you're joining, it matters little less. But look at it, right. Somebody who gets shouted by the founder, who can't shout back at the founder, who will he or she shout at you. So that dysfunctional way of org culture kind of permeates. So one thing you should look at is look up on attrition rate. You can look at LinkedIn, how many people have joined, how many people have left. You don't have to look for lots of years. You can just look at couple of years, right. You just look at couple of years and see, you know what? Let me just see how many people are joining, how many people left, how many people stayed for long, and then see where they have gone. If they're gone, If the young people have gone in for education, you know that is kind of a natural progression. If they joined another company, see what the person is, maybe you could go talk to them. I think you should, you should, you should look at all of these, right. Especially if you notice people leaving in less than a year. Those are a little bit of red flags. But it again also depends on how many people are there in the company to begin with. Like if there are only 6 people, where ours is like 30 odd people. It's very difficult to look at small companies. But dig in and you will definitely find something which says nice things about the founder. You can see whether the founder is commenting on something that the past employee has a post on past employee has written. So then you got to see that okay that the separation wasn't really bad. But that also gives you kind of an input in terms of look at the founder, look at their social media activity. What are they saying? What are they supporting? Some, although social media is a little bit of make-believe world, you can see patterns if you dig deep. So doesn't matter even if it is a small company, you should be able to leverage and see who else in this industry, what are things there. Because there's so much data that is already available, you can take some of these calls and see, right, how things are in this company vis-a-vis other companies or how people are coming in and moving out and things like that.",
