          "model_answer": "The lecture illustrates that a startup's health cannot be determined by a single dimension because both positive and negative realities can coexist publicly. The Ansh Nanda case shows that documented equity settlements and clear role splits (positive signals on paper) can exist alongside a culture of 2 AM meetings and idiosyncratic CEO schedules (negative cultural signals). Furthermore, the use of dark patterns in the app signals a focus on extraction that may extend to employee treatment. The lecture emphasizes that most students only encounter one dimension of a company depending on the source they read first, creating a diagnostic blind spot. Therefore, a complete evaluation requires integrating information about founder communication, observed work culture, role clarity, and personal reward structures, rather than anchoring to the first story or metric encountered.",
